# Viture Glasses — Gen1 HID protocol (Pro)

Applies when touching the Viture adapter: USB device detection, IMU pose
stream, control commands (recenter, brightness, display mode).

**Docs (if stuck):** https://github.com/bfvogel/viture-webxr-extension/blob/main/VITURE_PROTOCOL.md (Gen1 HID protocol write-up, works through Pro) ·
https://github.com/wheaney/XRLinuxDriver (protocol constants, display modes) ·
https://github.com/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/pull/1115 (SDK-free 3DoF virtual screen on Android — prior art) ·
https://github.com/elasticjava/viture-v2/blob/master/PROTOCOL.md (Gen2; reference only — Pro is Gen1) ·
https://www.viture.com/developer/glasses-sdk/glasses (official SDK — proprietary, do NOT vendor)

## Device facts

- Composite USB device on the same USB-C link as DP video.
  VID **0x35CA**, Viture Pro PID **0x101D**. Several HID interfaces — dedupe,
  IMU and MCU control are separate interfaces.
- Viture Pro: 1080p/eye, 2D modes 1920×1080 @ 60/90/120 (host-dependent),
  SBS 3840×1080 (we never drive SBS — 2D only). FOV ≈ 46° diagonal
  (~40°H × 23°V conservative), ~42 ppd.
- **No usable built-in 3DoF on Pro** — stabilization is always host-side.
- Android: video needs no permission; IMU/HID needs `UsbManager` runtime
  permission (user dialog or `device_filter.xml` vendor-id 13770). The XR
  permission broadcast action is `moe.n4tsu.dextop.xr.USB_PERMISSION` — do not
  reuse the Linux USB permission action. A dismissed dialog stays denied until
  an explicit UI re-request; do not ask again from a poll loop.

## Protocol notes (Gen1, community-documented)

- 64-byte HID reports, CRC-16 over the payload. **Framing discrepancy in the
  wild**: some docs say CRC-16/XMODEM, others measure CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE
  (poly 0x1021, init 0xFFFF) — test both on hardware before committing.
- Pose: enable IMU stream with command `0x15`; unsolicited `0xFFFC` reports
  carry big-endian float32 Euler angles at offset 18.
- Control (MCU interface): recenter command id `0x30`; display mode set
  `0x0124` (values 0x31 1080p60, 0x32 SBS, 0x33 90 Hz, 0x34 120 Hz — written
  twice, little-endian; read-back unreliable, current mode via `0x0142`);
  brightness `0x0122` (0–8). Commands ride the MCU interface, not the IMU one.
- EDID changes on mode switches (HPD low/high) — some phones keep stale DP
  state → black screen or 640×480. Treat mode switches as disconnect/reconnect.

## Invariants

- Never vendor the official `libglasses.so` / SDK zip — proprietary, GPL-incompatible.
- Never toggle 2D/SBS or refresh from Dextop (decision: 2D only).
- Pose arrives at ~120–500 Hz; fusion must tolerate gaps (sample rate not
  officially documented — measure on hardware).

## Symptom / cause / fix skeleton

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `0xFFFC` reports stop after a minute | IMU enable handshake not retried after interface re-open | Re-send `0x15` on USB re-attach; watch for interface claim conflicts |
| Commands ignored | Sent on IMU interface instead of MCU interface | Route control to MCU HID interface |
| CRC rejected on some units | XMODEM vs CCITT-FALSE framing variance | Detect per device; log raw frames on first contact |
| Black screen after refresh-rate change | Stale DP state across HPD/EDID change | Treat as reconnect; re-attach mirror on DisplayListener event |

